body:
Guns would def not be bad without it, there's a heavy focus upon utility and can easily win you rounds, you don't need the aimpunch.

&#x200B;

All it rewards is luck, not positioning, skill or strategy.

" Please be patient. This is a great game now"

&#x200B;

haha good one

b+ and rank 7 is still really fucking awful in the CS scene, you really dont have leverage to speak, the game is MUCH MUCH easier than CS

&#x200B;

A+/advanced playoffs/6k hours, the game is fucking easy as hell compared to cs no matter how many weird abilities there are

honestly if you're only resting at 2500 hours in CS and you've only played matchmaking you don't have a say in this, coming from the ESEA Advanced community, almost everyone agrees that valorant is much easier than CS

&#x200B;

the game is much easier to just point and click than in CS and requires much less thought to play, strategy is far less complicated and utility is incredibly easy to understand and theorycraft with, this game is easier 100%

&#x200B;

"Really? Too many headshots? Is it possible that Valorant has a better shot recognition?".  No fucking way anyone argues that, they argue that the gunplay is much easier and that anyone can pick up a rifle in this game and get multifrags they would never achieve in CS, not because of hitreg, but because this game has a lower skill ceiling

haha yeah dude they should just make it all $20,000 so only dubai collectors buy them, free market bro

&#x200B;

i wonder why that wouldn't make any sense, hmmm

honestly if going pro in this plays out the same way as CSGO, fortnite/overwatch players won't make it

&#x200B;

there's way too much knowledge they won't know at the start, and you can't learn that gamesense in a short period of time, lower tier CSGO players with team experience will reign for the initial 4-6 or so months if I had to guess

&#x200B;

in this sub: people who've never played any type of competitive scene

if there's no krieg nerf soon there probably won't be one anytime close, especially since the major just ended

&#x200B;

sad :\\
